From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:00:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: leave an idle external DCP down across
 a sleep

An external DCP with nothing attached is powered down at boot
(iomfb_m4_ext_idle_gate()). A sleep leaves it so, but the resume powers
up every external DCP it finds gated, as if the sleep had gated it. On
the J604 that retained RTKit wake of an idle DCP times out after every
suspend-to-idle, for both secondary DCPs:

  resume: power-up failed at RTKit wake: -62
  Retained DCP session quarantined: -62
  PM: failed to resume: error -62

and the failure is final for that DCP, so a display plugged in later
gets no session until a reboot.

Record whether iomfb_m4_ext_suspend_firmware() powered the DCP down for
this sleep and bring up only that one. One that was already idle stays
down, still marked idle, and the next request to its firmware powers it
up as before the sleep.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 339bd4d55d1f0773ea55c81e29634d195cb7659e)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 0a71e1fb2e..50f27b5732 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -356,6 +356,12 @@ struct iomfb_m4 {
 	 * by the fast path of iomfb_m4_ext_idle_wake(). Any power-up clears it.
 	 */
 	bool ext_idle_gated;
+	/*
+	 * An external DCP that iomfb_m4_ext_suspend_firmware() powered down for
+	 * the sleep, under the lock: only that one comes up again on resume. One
+	 * already down with nothing attached stays down until a request.
+	 */
+	bool ext_sleep_gated;
 	u64 ext_idle_cycles, ext_idle_wakes;
 	s64 ext_idle_off_us, ext_idle_on_us;
 	const char *ext_idle_why;
@@ -7177,8 +7183,13 @@ static int iomfb_m4_ext_suspend_firmware(struct iomfb_m4 *dcp)
 	if (dcp->rtkit)
 		apple_rtkit_flush_rx(dcp->rtkit);
 	mutex_lock(&dcp->lock);
-	if (!dcp->gated && iomfb_m4_ext_power_gate(dcp, "sleep"))
-		verdict = DCP_M4_FW_SLEEP_GATE_FAILED;
+	dcp->ext_sleep_gated = false;
+	if (!dcp->gated) {
+		if (iomfb_m4_ext_power_gate(dcp, "sleep"))
+			verdict = DCP_M4_FW_SLEEP_GATE_FAILED;
+		else
+			dcp->ext_sleep_gated = true;
+	}
 	if (verdict == DCP_M4_FW_SLEEP_OK) {
 		atomic_inc(&dcp->ext_pm_epoch);
 		WRITE_ONCE(dcp->ext_dart_down, true);
@@ -7266,9 +7277,15 @@ int iomfb_m4_resume(struct apple_dcp *owner)
 		if (dcp->rtkit)
 			apple_rtkit_flush_rx(dcp->rtkit);
 		atomic_inc(&dcp->ext_pm_epoch);
-		/* Down for a SoC power-down sleep: up again, in the new epoch. */
+		/*
+		 * Down for this sleep: up again, in the new epoch. Down before it
+		 * with nothing attached: stays down, as before the sleep; the
+		 * next request powers it up (dcp_m4_ext_up()).
+		 */
 		mutex_lock(&dcp->lock);
-		ret = dcp->gated ? iomfb_m4_ext_power_ungate(dcp, "resume") : 0;
+		ret = dcp->gated && dcp->ext_sleep_gated ?
+		      iomfb_m4_ext_power_ungate(dcp, "resume") : 0;
+		dcp->ext_sleep_gated = false;
 		mutex_unlock(&dcp->lock);
 		return ret;
 	}
-- 
2.43.0

